# HealthGuard Project Knowledge

## Project Overview

- HealthGuard is a Chrome extension focused on digital health.
- Core goals: manage screen time, reduce hearing risk, and nudge healthy habits.
- Privacy-first by design: user data stays local, with no outbound telemetry.

## Repository Shape

- Current repository is intentionally minimal and documentation-first.
- Main source of truth right now is `README.md`.
- Existing directories:
  - `docs/` for supporting documentation and assets.
  - `.cursor/rules/` for persistent AI guidance.

## Product Intent

- Track active browser usage with configurable daily and per-site limits.
- Monitor media loudness and support safe listening limits.
- Provide reminders for breaks, posture, hydration, and evening eye comfort.
- Offer local analytics and user-exportable history.

## Technical Direction

- Target platform is Chrome Extension Manifest V3.
- Expected runtime model:
  - service worker for background scheduling/state
  - content scripts for in-page behavior (overlay/audio hooks)
  - popup/options UIs for controls and reporting
- Favor modular utilities for time, storage, and audio calculations.

## Data and Privacy Constraints

- Treat privacy constraints as hard requirements, not optional enhancements.
- Prefer local-only persistence (`chrome.storage.local`, IndexedDB).
- Avoid introducing network calls unless explicitly requested by the user.
- Any analytics or logging should remain local by default.

## Editing and Collaboration Conventions

- Keep documentation clear, skimmable, and accurate to current repo state.
- When implementation files are added later, keep code structure consistent with documented architecture.
- Do not assume missing features are already implemented; verify file presence first.
- If behavior in docs and code diverges, update docs or flag mismatch clearly.

## Contribution Workflow Defaults

- Keep changes focused and reviewable.
- Prefer small, explicit commits when asked to commit.
- When unsure about architecture choices, ask before introducing irreversible structure.
